      "problem": "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(y+2)^{2}=-4x?$",
      "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(y+2)^{2}=-4x,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(y+2)^{2}=-4x\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is a leftward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(0,-2).$",
